<!--
  ssp5_policy.xml — SSP5-8.5 Fossil-Fueled Development (4–5 °C pathway)
  =======================================================================
  Narrative: rapid economic growth globally, driven by fossil fuels and
  heavy investment in human capital. Very high energy demand everywhere;
  near-total absence of binding climate policy. Renewables grow through
  economics after ~2040 but fossil fuels dominate through 2050.

  Carbon prices [$/tonne CO2]: negligible — no meaningful climate policy
    Africa: 3→8   Asia: 3→8   Europe: 8→20   LATAM: 4→10

  Renewable electricity standard: floor only — residual hydro + economics
    Africa: 18%→22%  Asia: 15%→20%  Europe: 30%→42%  LATAM: 42%→46%

  Key SSP5 distinction from SSP3:
    SSP3 = all regions weak (fragmented)
    SSP5 = globally coordinated fossil investment; strong institutions but
           choose NOT to price carbon; renewables eventually win on cost.
-->
